.TH CYAML_DICTIONARY_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_dictionary_remove \- remove and free a key from a dictionary node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_dictionary_remove(cyaml map, const char *key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the member with this key from the dictionary node map and
frees its value together with everything below it.  The remaining
members keep their order.  A cyaml_dictionary_iter cursor survives
the removal of any member except the one its next step reads (the
successor of the member it stands on).  So a walk may remove its
current member, but removing that successor invalidates the cursor.
See cyaml_dictionary_first(3).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - the member was removed and freed.
ccol_invalid_args   - map is NULL, or map is not a CYAML_DICTIONARY.
ccol_key_not_found  - the dictionary holds no such key.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_dictionary_set (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cyaml_list_remove (3)
